 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nJPEG images with EXIF data fail to load\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen trying to load JPEG images that contain EXIF metadata, the image processing fails with a KeyError. This affects images that have APP1 markers containing EXIF information.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom docx import Document\nfrom docx.shared import Inches\n\n# Create a new document\ndoc = Document()\n\n# Try to add a JPEG image with EXIF data\n# This will fail for images that contain EXIF metadata in APP1 markers\ndoc.add_picture('photo_with_exif.jpg', width=Inches(2))\n\ndoc.save('test_document.docx')\n```\n\nThe error occurs when the library tries to process JPEG images that contain EXIF data stored in APP1 markers. Images without EXIF data work fine, but those with camera metadata or other EXIF information cause the processing to fail.\n\n#### Expected Behavior\n\nJPEG images with EXIF metadata should be processed successfully, just like images without EXIF data.\n\n#### Actual Behavior\n\nProcessing fails with a KeyError when trying to access APP1 marker information from JPEG images containing EXIF data.\n</issue>\n",
